From: Hazel Smith <hazel@hazelesque.uk>
Subject: Wire in a non-prebuilt Java 21 toolchain via extra_toolchains

Bazel's default Java toolchain resolution downloads
@remote_java_tools_linux + @remotejdk11_linux from cdn.azul.com,
both of which are glibc-linked prebuilts.  On Chimera (musl libc)
they fail to execvp — the dynamic linker is /lib64/ld-linux-x86-
64.so.2 but musl's is /lib/ld-musl-x86_64.so.1, and the kernel
returns ENOENT for the missing interpreter (which surfaces as
"error=2 No such file or directory" pointing at javac, not the
interpreter).

The fix mirrors what scm-infra/copybara does in
tools/chimera_java_toolchain/BUILD and what Alpine's bazel7
APKBUILD ships as 0000-local-jdk.patch:

  - Add a `default_java_toolchain(...)` target that uses
    `@local_jdk//:jdk` for the runtime and source-builds the
    ijar / singlejar / TurbineDirect from the bazel tree itself.
    @local_jdk picks up JAVA_HOME (set to /usr/lib/jvm/java-21-
    openjdk in our cports template).
  - Register that toolchain via `common --extra_toolchains=...`
    in .bazelrc so it wins resolution over the prebuilt default.

`--tool_java_runtime_version=local_jdk` in EXTRA_BAZEL_ARGS is
still required to keep the @remotejdk11_linux download from
firing for the JavaToolchainCompileClasses action that builds
platformclasspath_classes.

diff --git a/.bazelrc b/.bazelrc
--- a/.bazelrc
+++ b/.bazelrc
@@ -92,3 +92,5 @@ test:ci-windows --test_env=JAVA_HOME
 test:ci-windows --test_env=TEST_INSTALL_BASE=C:/b/bazeltest_install_base
 test:ci-windows --test_env=REPOSITORY_CACHE=C:/b/bazeltest_repo_cache
 test:ci-windows --test_tag_filters=-no_windows,-slow
+
+common --extra_toolchains=//tools/chimera_java_toolchain:non_prebuilt_java_21_toolchain_definition
diff --git a/tools/chimera_java_toolchain/BUILD.bazel b/tools/chimera_java_toolchain/BUILD.bazel
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/chimera_java_toolchain/BUILD.bazel
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+load("@rules_java//toolchains:default_java_toolchain.bzl", "default_java_toolchain")
+
+default_java_toolchain(
+    name = "non_prebuilt_java_21_toolchain",
+    header_compiler_direct = "@remote_java_tools//:TurbineDirect",
+    ijar = "//third_party/ijar:ijar",
+    java_runtime = "@local_jdk//:jdk",
+    singlejar = "//src/tools/singlejar:singlejar",
+    source_version = "21",
+    target_version = "21",
+)
